# Generated project outputs
outputs/
searches/
replays/
benchmarks/
tools/ui_debug/generated/*.html
tools/ui_debug/generated/*.svg
tools/ui_debug/generated/*.png
_to_delete/
# Session scratch, same category as _to_delete/ above. `_xfer` is transit archives moving files
# between a cloud session and this machine; `_scratch` is built pages and one-off recordings
# kept for a second look. Everything in either is regenerable from a command in the tree -- a
# recording is `record_sow_offers.py --scenario X`, a page is its generator -- so committing
# them would only mean two copies, one of which nothing updates.
_xfer/
_scratch/
pilgrim_optimizer.egg-info/
*.tar.gz

# Scratch from generator sessions: experiments, probe renders, one-off scripts. Ignored rather than
# merely untracked, for two reasons. It is 198 MB, which makes it the one thing here that a
# `git add -A` must never reach. And its half-finished scripts were the only hits `ruff check
# --select F` reported in this working tree, while CI -- which sees tracked files -- was clean: a
# check that fails on scratch is a check you learn to skim past.
Claude outputs/

# Concept art: the folder is committed, these two parts of it are not.
#
# _reference/ holds third-party images kept for inspiration and never used in the game. Looking at
# one is fine; committing it would put somebody else's work in every clone forever, and the credit
# we would have to write beside it would probably name the wrong person -- a Pinterest link is a
# re-post, not an artist. The manifest records the URL so the reference survives without the file,
# and build_browser.py draws a card that links out when the file is not there.
ui/concept/_reference/
noun_wagon_7392556.svg

# The layout lab's build output. generate_layout_lab.py writes it on demand and the suites in
# tests/layout_lab/ read it from here; it is a build artefact, not a source file.
/out/
# The mutation suite in tests/layout_lab/ writes its working copies beside the page.
tests/layout_lab/_to_delete/
# Lab sessions exported from the layout lab, for local experimentation. Never committed: one
# exported WITH images is ~3.3 MB of base64 duplicating art already tracked under
# ui/board_v2/duty_actions/, and even the geometry-only export is a snapshot of somebody's
# session rather than a decision about the module. Keep the folder, ignore what lands in it.
ui/board_v2/layout_lab/sessions/

# Build artefacts the test suites write, beside the suite that writes them. accept*.mjs reads
# tests/layout_lab/lab.html when no page is given on the command line; mut44 writes its mutated
# copy next to it; mut45 and mut45b keep an on-disk stash of the generator and template they are
# mutating, so a run killed mid-mutation can put them back rather than leaving a broken tree and
# a suite that blames the code. None is a source file and all are regenerable, but until now
# running the suites left `git status` dirty -- which trains you to skim past it, and skimming
# past it is exactly how three pieces of art sat unrecorded for a day.
tests/layout_lab/lab.html
tests/layout_lab/lab_mut*.html
tests/layout_lab/.mut*_stash/
